# Performance

Redocly runs inside the JVM on GraalJS, so no Node.js is needed. By default GraalJS interprets the JavaScript,
which is fine for small descriptions and slow for large ones. The first line each goal logs names the engine in
use:

```
[INFO] Redocly 2.57.0 - JavaScript engine: GraalJS interpreter (add org.graalvm.polyglot:js-isolate-linux-amd64-community to the plugin dependencies for faster runs)
```

Enable the native isolate
-------------------------

For a 2–3× speed-up, add the native isolate named in that log line as a dependency **of the plugin** (not of
the project):

```xml
<plugin>
  <groupId>net.mwalser</groupId>
  <artifactId>openapi-toolkit-maven-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>${project.version}</version>
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.graalvm.polyglot</groupId>
      <artifactId>js-isolate-linux-amd64-community</artifactId>
      <version>${project.properties.getProperty("graalvm.version")}</version>
      <type>pom</type>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
</plugin>
```

Platforms: `linux-amd64`, `linux-aarch64`, `darwin-aarch64`, `windows-amd64`. The next build logs
`JavaScript engine: GraalJS native isolate`:

```sh
mvn validate | grep 'JavaScript engine'
# [INFO] Redocly 2.57.0 - JavaScript engine: GraalJS native isolate
```

Benchmarks
----------

These measurements compare cold lint runs on four cores:

| Description | Size | Node | Interpreter | Native isolate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Petstore | 17 KB | 0.06 s | 1.1 s | 0.4 s |
| Twilio API | 1.9 MB | 1.1 s | 18 s | 7 s |
| GitHub REST API | 12.9 MB | 6 s | 90 s | 44 s |

Engine selection
----------------

Which engine runs is decided once per build:

| Engine | When | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| GraalJS with runtime compilation | Maven runs on a GraalVM JDK whose version matches the embedded GraalJS (25) | none |
| GraalJS native isolate | the isolate dependency above is present | about 60 MB of downloads, 140 MB extracted to `~/.cache/org.graalvm.polyglot/` |
| GraalJS interpreter | otherwise (any JDK 21+) | none |

The engine and the Redocly bundle are initialized once per Maven JVM and reused by every goal and module, so the
warm-up (about 4 s for the interpreter, 1.4 s for the isolate) is paid once per build.

Isolate troubleshooting
-----------------------

- If the isolate dependency is present but cannot start, the build fails. Check that the artifact matches your
  platform and the GraalJS version in the plugin's [POM](https://github.com/mwalser/openapi-toolkit-maven-plugin/blob/main/pom.xml).
- On JDK 24+, add `--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED` to `.mvn/jvm.config` to suppress the Truffle
  native-access warning.
- The isolate extracts roughly 140 MB into `~/.cache/org.graalvm.polyglot/`. If the home directory is
  read-only, set `-Dpolyglot.engine.userResourceCache=<writable-directory>` in `.mvn/jvm.config`.
